From: KRdp displayless experiment <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] Give the desktop to one remote seat, and sequence the handover

Upstream places no limit on concurrent connections, and each one brings its own
virtual monitor, so a second client extends the desktop instead of taking it
over. Identical geometry merely confuses; differing geometry puts windows on one
monitor and leaves the other unreachable.

Closing the incumbent is not enough on its own. Its virtual output survives
until its teardown runs, and the output-lifecycle helper refuses to finish while
more than one RDP output exists - it reports "Timed out waiting for sole RDP
output" and fails the replacement's "up", which then tears the new session down
as well. Observed as a black screen on the first handover between clients of
differing DPI, with the incumbent's "down" arriving three seconds after the
replacement had already given up.

So close the incumbent, then poll until it has actually released the seat before
creating the new session. Once no wrapper holds a live connection, every
incumbent's onConnectionDestroyed has run, which means the helper has released
its output. Waiting is bounded: after ten seconds the replacement is activated
regardless, since a degraded desktop beats refusing the only client.

diff --git a/server/SessionController.cpp b/server/SessionController.cpp
index 8f352ef..6f97327 100644
--- a/server/SessionController.cpp
+++ b/server/SessionController.cpp
@@ -15,6 +15,7 @@
